<article class="env-lemma" id="08F6">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/08F6">Lemma <span data-tag="08F6">75.5.7</span>.</a> Let $S$ be a scheme. Let $X$ be an algebraic space over $S$. Let $E$ be an object of $D_\mathit{QCoh}(\mathcal{O}_ X)$. Then the map $E \to R\mathop{\mathrm{lim}}\nolimits \tau _{\geq -n}E$ of Derived Categories, Remark <a href="/tag/0H72" data-tag="0H72">13.34.5</a> is an isomorphism<a class="footnotemark" href="#a0001433010" id="a0001433010-mark"><sup>1</sup></a>. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Denote $\mathcal{H}^ i = H^ i(E)$ the $i$th cohomology sheaf of $E$. Let $\mathcal{B}$ be the set of affine objects of $X_{\acute{e}tale}$. Then $H^ p(U, \mathcal{H}^ i) = 0$ for all $p > 0$, all $i \in \mathbf{Z}$, and all $U \in \mathcal{B}$ as $U$ is an affine scheme. See discussion in Cohomology of Spaces, Section <a href="/tag/071Y" data-tag="071Y">69.3</a> and Cohomology of Schemes, Lemma <a href="/tag/01XB" data-tag="01XB">30.2.2</a>. Thus the lemma follows from Cohomology on Sites, Lemma <a href="/tag/0D6P" data-tag="0D6P">21.23.10</a> with $d = 0$. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>